Town phase 1b, the review's fixes: done (claude/town-phase1b, PR #1043; origin/main was already merged in, nothing new to merge).
PR body addition: .pr-body-add.md (what changed, the changed checks old -> new). No PR opened, no comments. About 1 h 50 min.

CI: green on b2a7e0bd, the last commit that changes code: `check` success, `e2e` success (21 jobs passed, 1 skipped). This commit
adds only this file.

Fixed (each with a test that fails on the old code, but where noted)
- S1 home's fetch ahead only while `queue` is empty (Home.tsx; every queue is home's frame with `queue` set: a boss battle's lobby, a
  match loading, a 1 v 1's search and versus). Its stop() aborts the file on its way. The town closing aborts its own load:
  loadBaked takes `closed` (Town.tsx `townClosed`), stops the fetches and decodes nothing more. The e2e check fails on the old code
  (35 pages fetched while the queue showed).
- S2 `TOWN_PICTURES.stallMs` (15 s): nothing arriving, the page showing -> abort and paint. My call: counted in bytes (the files are
  read as streams), not whole files. With files in parallel on a slow connection, no file may land for far longer than 15 s while
  all of them are still coming in; cutting those off would also throw away what was in flight, every visit. Hidden time doesn't count.
- S3 `reportBakedFallback` (problems.ts), once a page, kind `town-baked-fallback`, reasons manifest, file, decode, size, list, plus
  stall (S2's). The town closing mid-load, `?paintall` and a build with no baked town report nothing. Not counted apart on the
  server: it's among the errors on /admin/ops (a row a reason). No server change. docs/areas/ops.md has the lines.
- S4 home's fetch waits for `navigator.serviceWorker.controller` or `controllerchange`; at once if no worker is coming (install.ts
  `workerNever`: dev, no support, registration failed). The e2e waits on the controller and polls until every file is kept.
- S5 after a baked load, once a page: `idbShelf()?.clear()` and `brc.townTops` removed (the e2e seeds both and checks them gone).
- Data use: no fetch ahead on `saveData` or `effectiveType` slow-2g, 2g, 3g (`TOWN_PICTURES.homeFetchNotOn`).
- Nits: `adopt` returns whether it took the pages; `adoptOrKeep` (baked.ts) hands each picture to `keep` otherwise. The precache's
  town copy is in try/catch. The worker's TOWN_FILE is filled in by the build from `TOWN_FILE_PATH` (manifest.ts, made from
  BAKED_NAME), and a test ties them. A per-page memo: home never asks twice for a file. The town's requests are its own (the dedupe
  map is gone: it made the town wait on home's low-priority fetch, and can't live with abort). Dev: the manifest read fresh each town
  load; one bake at a time.
- "Parsed off the main thread if cheap": home doesn't read the manifest at all. The build hands the app each town's page names
  (`__TOWN_PAGES__`, from the same `filesOf`; about 3 KB in the main bundle); home fetches the manifest file at low priority only so
  the worker keeps it. The town's own load parses it under its card, as before.
- Pre-existing: the precache keeps only a 200, and under /assets/ never the app's page (nor copies one an older version kept): the
  install fails and the browser tries again. The lazy copy of a stopped request no longer leaves an unhandled rejection in the worker.

For the director
- No check that guards a rule in docs/rules/eric.md changed. No player-visible pixel or text. No still (nothing drawn changed).
- Measured, slowed phone, worker blocked, the files' fetch and decode over 6 visits: 0.7 to 1.6 s with the byte count, 0.75 to 1.2 s
  without. This container's runs vary that much by themselves; I saw no steady cost.
- Not verified here: iOS Safari (the review's "Not reached" still stands; the streamed read uses Response.body, there since Safari
  10.1, with res.blob() as the fallback). Worth Eric's one look at the town on his iPhone after the deploy.
- A page loaded past its worker (a hard reload) never gets a controller, so home fetches nothing ahead on that page; the town's own
  load still fetches.
- Local e2e in this container needed its own Playwright config (the pre-installed browser is a newer build than 1.56.1 expects);
  nothing of that is committed.
- Left for phase 1c, as briefed: S6 (pages kept twice) and the `loadSheetWaitMs` caps. 1c can reuse loadBaked's stall watch.
